183 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 74 0 R
/E (This file manages all storage and retrieval of note content. It initializes a FAISS flat index with 384 dimensions and maintains a parallel Python list called documents that holds the original text strings. The add_memory function converts incoming text to an embedding and adds it to both the index and the list simultaneously, keeping them synchronized. The search_memory function converts a query to an embedding and uses FAISS to find the top three most similar stored documents, returning their original text. This pairing of FAISS for vector search and a Python list for text retrieval is what powers the intelligent question-answering feature.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
