191 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (This is the central file that ties everything together. It sets up the FastAPI app, mounts the static directory so the CSS is accessible, and defines the route that serves the HTML page. The upload route accepts a file via multipart form data, checks whether it is a PDF or plain text file, extracts the text content accordingly using either PdfReader for PDFs or direct byte decoding for text files, and then calls add_memory to embed and store the content. A success message is returned once the file has been processed and stored.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
192 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (The ask route receives the user's query, passes it to search_notes to retrieve semantically relevant content, and then applies simple keyword-based logic to decide what portion of that content to return. Queries about names return filtered lines, queries about general information return the first 400 characters, and all other queries return the first 500 characters. The quiz route receives a topic, retrieves relevant notes using search_notes, passes the content to generate_quiz, and returns the formatted quiz as a JSON response. Both routes are concise and rely entirely on the tool and memory layers to do the heavy lifting.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
